  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_geo",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 456
        },
        "text": "World-space position, normal and the tangent frame. These feed every other block through **portals**, so no wire crosses the canvas."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_tri",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1374
        },
        "text": "Three projections (YZ, XZ, XY) blended by `|n|^sharpness` — no UVs, no stretching.\nAlbedo and height use the **Triplanar** kit; the normal map uses the Whiteout blend node and is converted from world to tangent space for the Lit master."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_mask",
        "position": {
          "x": 2260,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 2904
        },
        "text": "Moss wants **up-facing** surfaces: `up = smoothstep(0.1, 0.9, n·Y)`.\nA triplanar-projected noise texture (world space) breaks the mask into patches; *Moss Amount* scales the whole thing.\nThe **Height Blend** kit then lets the rock height push moss into crevices."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_mix",
        "position": {
          "x": 5368,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "The blend weight picks moss over rock for every output: **albedo** (moss tinted by the patch noise), **smoothness** (moss is rougher), **normal** (moss is softer: pulled 60 % towards flat), and cavity **occlusion** from the rock height."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 6726,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 90,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Surface outputs: base colour, tangent-space normal, metallic 0 (rock + moss are dielectrics), smoothness and cavity occlusion."
      }
    ],
